lisa-design:
- catalog-sync runs on the same controller runtime (one key, one worker, RequeueAfter = interval); Resync() forces a reload.
- Readers use CatalogProvider.Current()/Snapshot() (atomic pointer + channel closed on the next swap); first-load failure = nil + Ready() open; a later failure never clears the live catalog.
- A rejected head isn't reloaded until it moves; source errors retry with backoff (1s, capped at the poll interval).
- Timers live in internal/clock (NewTimer/NewTimerAt, absolute deadlines avoid a fake-clock race); controllers use clock.Clock.
- All git goes through gitsource (Head via ls-remote, Load), which redacts URL user info in errors.
- --catalog-dir reload polls a tree hash (no fsnotify: not on the allow-list); status is in memory (config never goes in the store).

